body: "# W6 touring-intelligence Fusion — COMPLETE\n\n**Date**: 2026-05-15\n**Wave**: W6 (touring-intelligence Fusion) of touring-premium-refactor-2026\n**Status**: COMPLETE — Option A revised (4-crate fusion, cortex excluded)\n**Workspace state**: GREEN (cargo check --workspace 0 errors)\n\n## Result\n\nFour intelligence crates fused into a single `touring-intelligence` crate;\nthe originals reduced to one-file re-export shims.\n\n| Source crate | LOC | Fate |\n|---|---|---|\n| touring-cognitive | 14,981 | touring-intelligence/src/reasoning/ |\n| touring-learning | 40,946 | touring-intelligence/src/rl/ |\n| touring-antt | 5,202 | touring-intelligence/src/ann/ |\n| touring-index | 2,734 | touring-intelligence/src/index/ |\n| touring-intelligence (fused) | 63,971 | new crate, 162 files |\n\nEach source crate is now an 8-9 line shim: `pub use touring_intelligence::<module>::*`.\n\n## Critical Discovery — touring-cortex excluded (Cargo cycle)\n\nThe plan called for fusing 4 crates INCLUDING touring-cortex. That is\nphysically uncompilable. touring-cortex depends on touring-hooks via 6 hook\nhandler modules (pre_read/pre_edit/pre_bash/post_read/post_edit/post_bash) +\nHookRuntime + IntentClassifier + PIIScanner. touring-hooks depends on\ncognitive/learning/antt. Fusing cortex creates the Cargo crate cycle\ntouring-intelligence <-> touring-hooks.\n\nResolution: touring-cortex is an orchestration-layer crate (it drives the\nhook pipeline). It stays standalone, deferred to W10 (touring-orchestration\nFusion). W6 fuses the 4 pure intelligence crates. touring-index (deferred\nfrom W5) was absorbed here.\n\nThe initial framing offered to Gabriel (\"the cortex->hooks edge is tiny, 4\nsymbols\") was based on an incomplete grep that missed the `use touring_hooks\nas hooks` alias. Corrected after the alias-aware grep revealed the deep\ncoupling. Gabriel chose Option A (4-crate fusion) on the corrected evidence.\n\n## Subtasks\n\n| # | Subtask | Outcome |\n|---|---|---|\n| W6.1 | Create touring-intelligence skeleton | taco-forge perfect-create-crate |\n| W6.2 | Move touring-cognitive -> reasoning/ | engineer, crate:: rewrites |\n| W6.3 | Move touring-learning -> rl/ | engineer, crate:: rewrites |\n| W6.4 | (touring-cortex) | EXCLUDED — Cargo cycle |\n| W6.5 | Move touring-antt -> ann/ + touring-index -> index/ | engineer |\n| W6.6 | lib.rs mount + 14-feature surface | reasoning/rl/ann/index |\n| W6.7 | Convert 4 crates to shims | 4 one-file shims + feature forwarding |\n| W6.8 | Validate | check/clippy/test/cycles all green |\n| W6.9 | Docs + checkpoint + memory + RL | this file |\n\n## Validation Gates\n\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---|\n| cargo check --workspace | 0 errors |\n| cargo check -p touring-intelligence (default) | 0 errors |\n| cargo test -p touring-intelligence | 1,758 PASS (1,407 lib + 351 integration) |\n| cargo test doctests | 26 PASS, 12 ignored, 0 failed |\n| cargo clippy (intelligence + 4 shims) | 0 issues |\n| consumer compile (server/hooks/cortex/generator/python) | 0 errors |\n| touring wiring cycles --min-depth 2 | 2 / depth 621 (unchanged vs W4/W5) |\n\n## Bugs fixed during execution (REGRA #0)\n\n- w6 rewriter idempotency-guard bug: it skipped legitimate `crate::rl::X`\n  references because touring-learning has a literal `rl` submodule (now\n  nested at `crate::rl::rl`). 5 imports needed `crate::rl::` -> `crate::rl::rl::`.\n- Missing `single-clustering` dependency in touring-intelligence Cargo.toml\n  (non-optional workspace dep used unconditionally by clustering/leiden.rs).\n- benches/ (6 files) and src/ doc-comments (39 refs) still referenced\n  `touring_learning::` / `touring_cognitive::` / `touring_antt::` — the\n  rewriter skipped the benches/ and doc-comment scopes. 48 refs corrected\n  via prefix rewrite.\n- 2 clippy errors surfaced under touring-intelligence strict lints:\n  module_inception (`rl::rl`) + type_complexity (GLOBAL_QTABLE LazyLock).\n\n## Pre-existing breakage (NOT W6 regressions)\n\n- `cargo check -p touring-intelligence --no-default-features` has 18 errors —\n  feature-gating debt inherited from touring-learning, whose `default` always\n  carried 9 features; the bare build was never validated upstream. Default +\n  workspace builds are 0 errors. Deferred to W11 (Test Debt Repayment).\n\n## Macrocycle 621 — NOT eliminated (not in scope for Option A)\n\nThe W6 plan claimed \"macrociclo 618 ELIMINADO\". This is not achievable by\nOption A — nor by the original plan. The 621-module cycle spans ~15 crates\n(foundation, hooks, analysis, resource-monitor, server, wasm, assists,\ninferlets, definitions, activity, ast) — a workspace-wide module-coupling\nproblem, not a cognitive/cortex/learning one. It is matter for W8/W9\ninternal-split waves plus a dedicated cycle-decomposition wave.\n\n## Files\n\n```\ncrates/touring-intelligence/           NEW — 63,971 LOC, 162 files, 4 modules\n  Cargo.toml                           merged deps + 14 features\n  src/lib.rs                           mounts reasoning/rl/ann/index\n  src/{reasoning,rl,ann,index}/         fused source\n  tests/ (15 files) + benches/ (6 files)  relocated\n\ncrates/touring-cognitive/              -> SHIM (8-line lib.rs)\ncrates/touring-learning/               -> SHIM (9-line lib.rs)\ncrates/touring-antt/                   -> SHIM (9-line lib.rs)\ncrates/touring-index/                  -> SHIM (8-line lib.rs)\ncrates/touring-cortex/                 UNCHANGED — standalone, deferred to W10\n\nscripts/touring_premium_refactor_2026/\n  w6_rewrite_crate_paths.py            string-aware Rust path rewriter\n```\n\n## Next wave\n\nW7 (touring-bindings Fusion) — depends on W3 only, already unblocked.\nW10 (touring-orchestration Fusion) should absorb touring-cortex.\n"
